<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="no"?>
<!-- =====================================================================
     PRJEDU_net - AyMON example: the engine talks to the office world.
     Part 1: mail. Nothing to install.

     One engine, two documents, real SMTP on a loopback socket:

       PLT/S00   a tank with a level alarm, and a MAIL CONNECTION: when
                 the level alarm comes and goes, the engine writes a mail.
                 A mail is a WRITE to a point, its outcome comes back into
                 the same point, and the page shows both.
       MBX/S00   the other end: a small mail server written in script on
                 top of PRO.raw, so the example needs no mail account and
                 nothing installed. It keeps what it receives and hands it
                 to the page. Point CN_MAIL at your own mail server and
                 the same mails go to a real inbox (README).

     The mail side (PRO.smtp) lives in the engine module AyLIB_net,
     beside AyXDB in ../../../bin. It is attached the first time a <con> names
     PRO.smtp: no xdb_lib needed.

     Needs engine 4.3.4.565 or later (pro_onaccept: a server in script
     that speaks first).

     Run:  run.bat,  then open  http://127.0.0.1:8114/
     ===================================================================== -->
<xdb id="XDB" xdb_lib="AyPRO" xdb_log="4" log_cfg="0x39C0" log_lnk="%PRJ%/log/XDB.log"
     sta="0x0300" tid="S01">
	<config>
		<doc id="MBX/S00" sta="0x0300" src="%DB%/db_MBX.xml" desc="the mail server - SMTP in script" />
		<doc id="FTP/S00" sta="0x0300" src="%DB%/db_FTP.xml" desc="the file server - FTP in script" />
		<doc id="PLT/S00" sta="0x0300" src="%DB%/db_PLT.xml" desc="the plant, its mail connection and the page" />
	</config>
	<data>
	</data>
</xdb>
